# ── Environment variables ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env.local` for local dev, and set the same keys in the Vercel
# dashboard (Project → Settings → Environment Variables) for deploys.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are exposed to the browser; everything else (e.g.
# RESEND_API_KEY) is server-only — never prefix a secret with NEXT_PUBLIC_.

# Canonical site origin. Used for metadataBase, canonical URLs, the sitemap,
# robots.txt, and JSON-LD. Defaults to https://praduansaha.com when unset
# (see src/lib/site.ts), so it's optional in production if that domain is live.
# On Vercel you can point it at the deployment URL for preview builds, e.g.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-project.vercel.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://praduansaha.com

# ── Contact form (Resend) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Server-only — powers the /contact message form (src/app/actions/contact.ts).
# Create an API key at resend.com. RESEND_API_KEY is a SECRET: put it in
# .env.local and in Vercel (Project → Settings → Environment Variables); the
# repo is public, so never commit the real value.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# Where submissions are delivered — your inbox. hey@ forwards to Gmail already.
CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=hey@praduansaha.com
# The verified Resend sender the mail is FROM. Must be on a domain you've
# verified in Resend — use a SUBDOMAIN (e.g. contact@send.praduansaha.com) so it
# doesn't clash with the ImprovMX MX that's already on praduansaha.com.
CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=
